# tools/hunk_edit_finger_view_witness.rish — the finger-driven Photos editor on metal (HUNK51).
#
# Season A (Hardware & Right-to-Repair) · waymark HUNK · journey Photos app · rung HUNK51.
# Design read: active-designing/20260813-205200_hunk-edit-finger-view-exploration.md.
# Teacher, thanked clean-room: the touch editor of a photo app (iCloud Photos / Google Photos) — a finger taps a tool
# or swipes the history and the picture on glass follows (concept only, siloed).
#
# HUNK50 reads a finger into a gesture but moves no cursor; HUNK49 owns a cursor and paints it but takes a gesture
# already made. This rung binds both to ONE cursor, the exact parallel of HUNK47 for scroll: finger_up classifies the
# touch and, when a gesture fires, applies it to the view's cursor, and paint renders exactly that cursor — so the glass
# can never drift from what the finger just did. The selftest drives the surface by finger events and proves a tap on
# the strip repaints the edit on glass, swipes repaint the walked history, a tap off the strip fires nothing, paint
# never drifts from the view, and a bad grid or cell refuses at open. No network, no key, no funds.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/hunk_edit_finger_view_witness.rish

say "hunk-edit-finger-view: Language EN — HUNK51 binds HUNK50's finger classifier and HUNK49's painted view to one cursor: a finger edits the picture, the glass repaints."
say "hunk-edit-finger-view: Style Radiant — a device hands raw finger coordinates to one object and watches the picture change; the touch surface and the glass share one history, so the picture can never drift from the finger."
say "hunk-edit-finger-view: Lens TAME — the object routes a finger through two proven seams into one shared cursor; no new arithmetic, no new clamp, no new render primitive; refusals only the sub-surfaces' own; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "brushstroke/bin/edit_finger_view"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p brushstroke/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build brushstroke/edit_finger_view.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "hunk-edit-finger-view: build failed — ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "hunk-edit-finger-view: selftest exited non-zero — ${selftest.out}"

# The claim checks use Rishi's native `contains` — the output is a Rishi value, never interpolated into a shell
# single-quoted string, so an apostrophe in the GREEN line can never break a check (the loom for REDS #76).
let out = trim selftest.out
say "hunk-edit-finger-view: ${out}"

assert out contains "GREEN edit-finger-view" else "hunk-edit-finger-view: selftest did not print the GREEN edit-finger-view line"
assert out contains "a tap on the strip cell repaints the flip on glass" else "hunk-edit-finger-view: a tap did not repaint the edit on glass"
assert out contains "a left swipe repaints the source and a right swipe the flip" else "hunk-edit-finger-view: swipes did not repaint the walked history"
assert out contains "a tap off the strip fires nothing" else "hunk-edit-finger-view: a tap off the strip did not fire nothing"
assert out contains "paint equals a direct view.paint cell-for-cell (no drift)" else "hunk-edit-finger-view: the painted picture drifted from the cursor"
assert out contains "each refuse at open by name" else "hunk-edit-finger-view: a bad grid, cell, or swipe did not refuse at open"

say "hunk-edit-finger-view: GREEN — the Photos editor takes a finger: a tap repaints the edit on glass, swipes repaint the walked history, a tap off the strip does nothing, the picture never drifts from the finger, and bad geometry refuses at open; no network, no key, no funds."
